202,"Establishment of a centralized, multi-factor authentication (MFA) system can significantly enhance user experience and security. Referral role: A user admin who needs to onboard new employees and ensure MFA is set up correctly. To facilitate the referral process, users can access the MFA system and create a new user account. They can then navigate to the setup page and follow the prompts to activate the MFA mechanism. Additionally, the user can refer an existing employee, and through a shared access link, they can enable the MFA system for the referred user. This setup ensures seamless two-factor authentication, making it easier for users to protect their digital credentials."
