230,"""Helping someone succeed at our team is more rewarding than any profit. When a colleague shares a solution or best practice with us, it's like a valuable asset we've acquired. Here's how to properly refer in a team setting: Share relevant information or expertise with others, but do not: - Share proprietary details - Take credit or claim sole responsibility - Break confidentiality agreements or company policies When providing help, be transparent and acknowledge the other person's contribution. Your role is to support and collaborate, not to profit from the situation."
